<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikita Khrushchev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1894–1971</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikita Khrushchev was leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> from the mid-1950s to 1964, as first secretary of the Communist Party and, from 1958, also premier. His secret speech of 1956 denounced Stalin and began a partial thaw, while he crushed the Hungarian uprising and brought the world close to nuclear war in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis">Cuban Missile Crisis</a> of 1962. He was removed by his colleagues in 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikita-khrushchev.jpg" alt="Nikita Khrushchev" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TASS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1956_Press_Photo_Communist_Party_Secretary_Nikita_S._Khrushchev_in_Moscow_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
